<http://data.silknow.org/object/234b6f11-a41f-338f-965b-65580c38f3b2/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "A man’s coat of green and pink shot silk with a 2-piece, 3¼-inch (8.2 cm) turned-down collar, pointed at the back, and curving 2-piece sleeves ending in mariner’s cuffs, 3⅛ inches (8.3 cm) deep.  The fronts curve from neck to hem with pleats 3¾ inches (9.5 cm) deep, below the hip set beside the centre back.  Each front has a pocket and rectangular pocket flap; the centre-back seam is open below the hip.   The back and sleeves are lined with unbleached fustian, the pockets with blue linen, the fronts, skirts and pocket flaps with plain-weave silk.  There are 11 worked buttonholes along the left front edge and 2 on each cuff.  Only the 4th and 5th buttonhole from the top have been cut.  There are 11 self-covered buttons on the right front, 4 below the pockets and 1 at the hem and top of the pleats.  Only 1 button remains on the right cuff."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/234b6f11-a41f-338f-965b-65580c38f3b2> .

